    {
      "topLeftX": 84,
      "topLeftY": 104,
      "bottomRightX": 193,
      "bottomRightY": 124,
      "content": "## Names of jobs",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 82,
      "topLeftY": 134,
      "bottomRightX": 599,
      "bottomRightY": 167,
      "content": "Some names of jobs describe what the person does very clearly. For example, taxi-driver.\nThe two nouns combine to make one word and are called compounds.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 168,
      "bottomRightX": 342,
      "bottomRightY": 183,
      "content": "Sometimes they are joined: shopkeeper",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 183,
      "bottomRightX": 360,
      "bottomRightY": 199,
      "content": "Sometimes they have a hyphen: life-guard",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 199,
      "bottomRightX": 412,
      "bottomRightY": 216,
      "content": "Sometimes they stay as two words: English teacher",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 83,
      "topLeftY": 232,
      "bottomRightX": 441,
      "bottomRightY": 250,
      "content": "### Say what each of these people does in their job:",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 113,
      "topLeftY": 265,
      "bottomRightX": 384,
      "bottomRightY": 281,
      "content": "Example: taxi-driver: A taxi-driver dives taxis.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 83,
      "topLeftY": 281,
      "bottomRightX": 518,
      "bottomRightY": 329,
      "content": "Note: In American English programme is always spelt 'program'. In British English this spelling is used only in connection with computers. It is both a noun and a verb.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 151,
      "topLeftY": 337,
      "bottomRightX": 528,
      "bottomRightY": 388,
      "content": "tourist guide firefighter bookseller taxi-driver\ncomputer programmer dressmaker film director newsreader\nscience teacher bank manager project manager",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 83,
      "topLeftY": 400,
      "bottomRightX": 499,
      "bottomRightY": 433,
      "content": "In 'taxi-driver' there is no 's' at the end of taxi. When nouns are used as adjectives, They are always singular.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 83,
      "topLeftY": 447,
      "bottomRightX": 533,
      "bottomRightY": 466,
      "content": "### Find other examples in the list. Can you think of any others?",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 85,
      "topLeftY": 486,
      "bottomRightX": 153,
      "bottomRightY": 505,
      "content": "## Qualities",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 82,
      "topLeftY": 515,
      "bottomRightX": 584,
      "bottomRightY": 550,
      "content": "If you want to be a teacher you must be patient. In an advertisement the employer will ask for someone who shows patience.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 83,
      "topLeftY": 569,
      "bottomRightX": 627,
      "bottomRightY": 589,
      "content": "### Use the adjectives and nouns below to make sentences about other jobs.",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 137,
      "topLeftY": 602,
      "bottomRightX": 258,
      "bottomRightY": 668,
      "content": "polite politeness\ndiligent diligence\nfriendly friendliness\nable ability",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 314,
      "topLeftY": 603,
      "bottomRightX": 530,
      "bottomRightY": 668,
      "content": "patient patience\nconscientious conscientiousness\nconfident confidence\ncomputer literate computer literacy",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 83,
      "topLeftY": 685,
      "bottomRightX": 469,
      "bottomRightY": 703,
      "content": "### What do you think these underlined phrases mean?",
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 83,
      "topLeftY": 713,
      "bottomRightX": 318,
      "bottomRightY": 731,
      "content": "Applicants will have good people skills.",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 83,
      "topLeftY": 731,
      "bottomRightX": 408,
      "bottomRightY": 746,
      "content": "The successful candidate will have a telephone manner.",
